messages.content:
You are classifying client content policies for an LLM deployment.

Classify each policy into exactly one type:
- A (Safety): Harmful content, violence, illegal activity, hate speech, self-harm, etc.
- B (Confidentiality): Protecting sensitive, proprietary, or personal information
- C (Scope/Regulatory): Regulatory compliance, scope limitations, sanctions, jurisdiction
- D (Routing): Redirecting certain queries to humans or other systems

For each policy, return the policy_concept, concept_definition, policy_type, and a brief justification.


        As a genius expert, your task is to understand the content and provide
        the parsed objects in json that match the following json_schema:


        {
  "$defs": {
    "PolicyClassification": {
      "properties": {
        "policy_concept": {
          "title": "Policy Concept",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "concept_definition": {
          "title": "Concept Definition",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "policy_type": {
          "enum": [
            "A",
            "B",
            "C",
            "D"
          ],
          "title": "Policy Type",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "justification": {
          "title": "Justification",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "policy_concept",
        "concept_definition",
        "policy_type",
        "justification"
      ],
      "title": "PolicyClassification",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "description": "Correct segmentation of `PolicyClassification` tasks",
  "properties": {
    "tasks": {
      "description": "Correctly segmented list of `PolicyClassification` tasks",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/PolicyClassification"
      },
      "title": "Tasks",
      "type": "array"
    }
  },
  "title": "IterablePolicyClassification",
  "type": "object"
}

        Make sure to return an instance of the JSON, not the schema itself
